<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11839" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŭlīna</span></b>  (old orthogr. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŏlīna</span></b> , acc. to
				<i><span class="en">Non. p. 55, 18 sq.</span></i>),
		ae, f.
		Sanscr. çar, çri, to cook, mix,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a kitchen</i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop., <i><span class="en">Plaut. Most.
				1, 1, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Truc. 2, 7, 53</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 13, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				15, 18, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 114, 26</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Petr. 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 1,
				5, 73</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 5, 80</span></i>; cf. of <i>a
				portable kitchen</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep.
				78, 23</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 3,
			250</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Culina vocatur locus, in
			quo epulae in funere comburuntur, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest.
				p. 65, 12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>, <i>food, fare,
			victuals</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Murenā praebente domum, Capitone
					culinam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 1, 5, 38</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">Juv. 5, 162</span></i>; <i><span class="en">14, 14</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
